{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310671,"nonce":"aZfZk7FKKRoGT/VB9FyyGEs9C8A=","title":"2026-09-24 b85cfd91+267fa908 (624-\u003e635) — switch patterns (extractor/binder/object/array) desugar to a guarded wildcard in switch.rs; ...","message":"**b85cfd91 + 267fa908, conformance 624 -\u003e 635, 0 lost.** Issues f2864ffd (patterns), 23cd17e5 (Array\u003cDynamic\u003e literals); open follow-ups a4f00f7 (GADT `P:C\u003cPR\u003e` ctor matches everything), 1a5a1a8 (Array\u003cAbstract\u003e of literals omitting optional typedef fields → wrong layout; blocks Issue3088).\n\n- **Pattern design**: `switch.rs::pattern_guard_parts` turns Array/Object/Bind/Extractor patterns into (test on the subject, bindings) in PARSER-AST space; `build_extractor_case` makes a wildcard case + guard + binding prelude. A nested enum constructor → an inner `switch` binding fresh `__patternN_i` names, so the REAL matcher does enum tests. `switch [a, b]` → match elementwise against the literal's items (indexing it reads every element as the FIRST element's type). Parser: `Pattern::Extractor.value` is a Pattern; `Pattern::Bind`; `{...}` becomes Pattern::Object only when a plain literal parse fails or has an Assign field.\n- **A return inside a switch EXPRESSION did not type an un-annotated function** (resolve.rs had no Switch arm in find_return_type_in_expression). Cheap, broad.\n- **Array\u003cDynamic\u003e literals: box REFERENCES only, keep scalars raw.** Boxing ints broke GenericCallTypeArgs (erased T=Int reads raw) and `Type.createInstance(A, [true])` (ctor wrappers read raw). **You cannot unwrap at runtime**: `tag_is_known` accepts any header word \u003e 100, so a raw class instance or HaxeString pointer looks like a box. Hence literal retyping skips EXTERN callees (`callee_is_extern`).\n- Haxe 4.3.6 REJECTS `case CInt(_ \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 _ \u003c 12)` (Issue11157 is from a newer Haxe) — verify corpus syntax with `haxe --run` before implementing it.\n- Remaining parser gaps (from the 16): arrow params `(?a:Int=1) -\u003e` (ArrowParam has no optional/default; plan: parser emits a Function literal when present), `(() -\u003e 1 : () -\u003e Int)`, postfix `!` via `@:op(A!)`, `a in b` operator, map comprehension `=\u003e` in parens, TestNullCoalescing.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_dynamic_array_elements_stored_raw]], [[feedback_moved_rows_are_where_regressions_hide]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_pattern_guard_desugar_and_dynamic_literals` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}